  "title": "A Fano atom with a line removed is transparent",
  "subject": "What a Fano atom sends through its cuts when one of its lines is removed",
  "conclusion": "In every knot space, a Fano atom with any one of its lines removed sends the free relation through each of its cuts, so what it changes there does not depend on which line went. The proof joins the project's cut theorem (closed sides act as their lost elements, up to signs), the fact that the plain Fano plane is the only signed Fano knot, and an exhaustive freeness check.",
